Under symmetric $+1/{-}1$ rewards, EFE over-observes relative to Planning ($+0.38$ vs.\ $+0.48$ reward, seed-level Welch $p{=}1.1{\times}10^{-5}$). Success-tuned agents push this trade-off to $99.5\%$ success at $+0.01$ reward. Posterior-vote matches Planning on all three metrics. Epistemic-only matches Planning on observations and success here because information gain clears the $0.1$ observation cost, but commits immediately on Tiger, Diagnosis, Bandit, and Tileworld (\texttt{results\_\allowbreak summary.csv}, Appendix~\ref{app:full_tables}).

At the post-first-observation belief, a second observation has zero instrumental value: a disconfirming outcome returns belief to the tie point. Proposition~\ref{prop:nearopt}'s resulting ceiling is $w^*_{\mathrm{over}}\approx1.01$ reward units per nat, below the implemented weight's $1.44$ (Table~\ref{tab:alpha_eta}). Testbed is a boundary case of the proposition's strict asymmetry assumption, and Appendix~\ref{app:theory_thresholds} distinguishes this two-step calculation from measured behavior at $H{=}4$.

