\section{Proper-Scoring Calibration}
\label{app:calibration}

To assess terminal beliefs separately from decisions, we use the proper log score $\ln b(s^\star)$ and Brier score $\sum_s(b(s)-\mathbf{1}[s=s^\star])^2$, where $s^\star$ is the true state \citep{gneiting2007}. Log-score probabilities are floored at $10^{-12}$. Inspection scores average over binary component beliefs, not the joint state. These rules measure overall belief quality, combining calibration and informativeness: a uniform prior and a posterior after perfect observation can both be calibrated, despite different expected scores.

Table~\ref{tab:calibration} compares Planning, EFE, and a reference over five seeds, with $500$ episodes per seed except $200$ for Inspection-N16. The reference on Tiger, Diagnosis, and Bandit is SARSOP's in-simulator alpha-vector policy \citep{kurniawati2008}. Our SARSOP build does not scale practically to Inspection, whose reference is Planning+IG at the atlas's higher canonical budget (Appendix~\ref{app:w_atlas}).

